  "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$, $y$, and $z,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0x-8y+4z=-\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ 0x+5y+\\frac{2}{3}z=8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3}y+4z=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy simplifying, we obtain \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-8y+4z=-\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ 5y+\\frac{2}{3}z=8 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3}y+4z=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
